<title>USA: Groen says Shanghai Energy buys gyroplanes.</title>
<headline>Groen says Shanghai Energy buys gyroplanes.</headline>
<dateline>SALT LAKE CITY 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Groen Brothers Aviation Inc said Tuesday they had signed a contract for sale of 200 Hawk III commercial gyroplanes to The Shanghai Energy and Chemicals Corp.</p>
<p>Groen said the $40 million contract spans the three years it will take to build and deliver the planes. First payments are contingent upon GBA qualifying its Hawk gyroplanes for flight in China, the company said.</p>
<p>Shanghai Energy plans to establish an air taxi company in China, using the gyroplanes as its main form of transport, Groen said.</p>
</text>
